# Single source of shellcheck configuration. shellcheck walks up from each checked file
# to find this, so the pre-commit gate and the lint-after-edit hook read the same settings
# without either passing flags — which is the point. They previously disagreed: the hook
# ran at default severity while nothing else ran shellcheck at all.

# One directive, because .shellcheckrc takes `disable=` but NOT `severity=` — severity is
# a CLI flag only (checked against shellcheck 0.11.0). Naming codes is more precise than a
# threshold anyway.
#
#   SC1091 — sourced fragments (agentview modules, hook libraries) are resolved by their
#            loader at runtime, not by a path shellcheck can follow
#   SC2016 — single-quoted jq/awk programs, where NOT expanding is the whole point
#   SC2015 — `A && B || C`, used deliberately for cleanup-on-failure
#
# The last two are info-level and systematic across this repo. Everything else, at every
# severity, is enforced.
disable=SC1091,SC2016,SC2015
